      "Start with replacement cadence. A typical tarp costs $80 to $250 and lasts one to three winters in a climate with real snow and freeze-thaw cycles. UV exposure, ice, wind, and the weight of standing water degrade the material quickly. Replacing a $150 tarp every two years costs $75 per year before anything else. A standard mesh safety cover at $1,500 with an 18-year warranty costs about $83 per year, and a premium cover at $2,500 over 25 years costs $100 per year. The upfront gap is large, but the annual gap is surprisingly small, and the safety cover delivers far more along the way.",
